Someone asked for Google sign-in on <%= @app_name %><%= " (#{@host})" if @host %>.

The app already draws the "Sign in with Google" button; it opens a setup notice
until the OAuth client is in place. Two steps finish it:

1. Add this redirect URI to the shared production OAuth client
   (Google Cloud project <%= @oauth_project %>, admin@ Chrome profile; Steffon's lane):

<% if @redirect_uri -%>
   <%= @redirect_uri %>
<% else -%>
   (none yet: the app names no canonical host. Set APP_HOST, or
   Studio.google_canonical_host, to its production hostname; the URI is then
   https://<that host>/auth/google_oauth2/callback)
<% end -%>

2. Set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET on the app, then restart it.

Once both are set, the button posts straight to Google. This request is sent at
most once per app per day. The URI above comes from the app's configuration,
never from the request that asked.

Guide: studio-engine docs/GOOGLE_AUTH_SETUP.md
